    {
      "patch": "diff --git a/server/server.go b/server/server.go\nindex 989b7a75..026582a6 100644\n--- a/server/server.go\n+++ b/server/server.go\n@@ -1141,6 +1141,18 @@ func (s *Server) buildCreateMessageParams(conversationID string, message llm.Mes\n \t\t}\n \t\tud = udMap\n \t}\n+\t// Stamp the working directory the conversation had when this agent message\n+\t// was emitted, so the UI can resolve file references in it against the cwd\n+\t// of its time rather than the conversation's current one (which later\n+\t// change_dir calls move). The loop wrapper carries the live toolset cwd in\n+\t// the context; only assistant messages can carry model-authored references.\n+\tif cwd := emissionCwdFromContext(ctx); cwd != \"\" \u0026\u0026 message.Role == llm.MessageRoleAssistant {\n+\t\tif udMap, ok := ud.(map[string]any); ok {\n+\t\t\tudMap[\"cwd\"] = cwd\n+\t\t} else if ud == nil {\n+\t\t\tud = map[string]any{\"cwd\": cwd}\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n \t// End-of-turn agent and error messages mean the agent has finished. Fold\n \t// the agent_working=false flip into the message-INSERT Tx so a single\n \t// OnCommit hook emits one list-patch carrying both, instead of two\n",
      "comment": "Stamping happens where user_data is assembled: assistant messages fold the context-carried cwd into the JSON bag (merging with error metadata when present). User and system messages are deliberately unstamped — they carry no model-authored references."
    },
    {
      "patch": "diff --git a/server/convo.go b/server/convo.go\nindex 38573920..4e49dc41 100644\n--- a/server/convo.go\n+++ b/server/convo.go\n@@ -310,6 +310,15 @@ func NewConversationManager(conversationID string, database *db.DB, baseLogger *\n \t\tstreamPub:              streamPub,\n \t\tonStateChange:          onStateChange,\n \t}\n+\t// Stamp the conversation's current working directory onto every message\n+\t// recorded through this manager (loop turns and direct calls alike) so\n+\t// the UI can resolve file references in a message against the cwd of its\n+\t// time; later change_dir calls cannot re-point older references. Cwd()\n+\t// takes cm.mu, which no recordMessage caller holds.\n+\tcm.recordMessage = func(ctx context.Context, msg llm.Message, usage llm.Usage, otherUsage []llm.PurposedUsage) error {\n+\t\treturn recordMessage(contextWithEmissionCwd(ctx, cm.Cwd()), msg, usage, otherUsage)\n+\t}\n+\treturn cm\n }\n \n // broadcastStream tags data with the conversation ID and fans it out to both\n",
      "comment": "The stamp enters via a wrapper installed at construction, so *every* recording path through the manager gets it — loop turns and direct calls (cancel's end-turn marker) alike. `Cwd()` takes `cm.mu`, which no caller of `recordMessage` holds; the end-turn path holds the lifecycle mutex, a different lock."
